From 44c1a37dcee729c1b1517ca1667f11711d31826f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 22:29:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 49/50] demux: rawvid: fix wrong pcr after a seek

Control() is a bare demux_vaControlHelper() call, and the helper implements
DEMUX_SET_POSITION and DEMUX_SET_TIME as a plain vlc_stream_Seek(): the
stream moves, but the pcr date is left untouched and keeps counting from
where it was before the seek.

DEMUX_GET_TIME goes through the same helper and is derived from the byte
offset, so it stays correct, and the timestamps the demuxer emits no longer
agree with the time it reports. Playback of the track itself survives
because the input resets the PCR on every seek, but slave ES do not:
SlaveDemux() paces external subtitles from the master DEMUX_GET_TIME, so
after a seek they are shifted by the accumulated error, or dropped for
being too late or too early.

The helper seeks frame aligned, so the new offset gives back the frame
number: set the date from it, which is exact and matches what Demux() would
have accumulated. Note that this does not make seeking in a YUV4MPEG2
stream any more precise, as the per frame headers are not accounted for in
the frame size the helper aligns on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/rawvid.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/rawvid.c b/modules/demux/rawvid.c
index f16e07eea5..ba38152776 100644
--- a/modules/demux/rawvid.c
+++ b/modules/demux/rawvid.c
@@ -443,7 +443,29 @@ static int Control( demux_t *p_demux, int i_query, va_list args )
                                                     p_sys->pcr.i_divider_den;
 
     /* XXX: DEMUX_SET_TIME is precise here */
-    return demux_vaControlHelper( p_demux->s, 0, -1, i_bps,
-                                   p_sys->frame_size, i_query, args );
+    int i_ret = demux_vaControlHelper( p_demux->s, 0, -1, i_bps,
+                                       p_sys->frame_size, i_query, args );
+    if( i_ret != VLC_SUCCESS )
+        return i_ret;
+
+    switch( i_query )
+    {
+        case DEMUX_SET_POSITION:
+        case DEMUX_SET_TIME:
+            /* The helper only moved the stream: resync the pcr accumulator,
+             * else it would keep counting from before the seek and drift
+             * away from the byte derived DEMUX_GET_TIME. The helper seeks
+             * frame aligned, so the offset gives back the frame number. */
+            date_Set( &p_sys->pcr,
+                      (int64_t)( vlc_stream_Tell( p_demux->s )
+                                 / p_sys->frame_size )
+                      * CLOCK_FREQ * p_sys->pcr.i_divider_den
+                      / p_sys->pcr.i_divider_num );
+            break;
+        default:
+            break;
+    }
+
+    return VLC_SUCCESS;
 }
 
